// A low cave where an ember paces; the stone is by the cave's far wall, and the bloom that grows from it puts the ember out; a crumbling bridge over acid past the spouts.
name Quench
rule B1234/S012345678
steps 3
hint An ember paces the low cave. The stone is on its floor, by the far wall, and the wall cut the bloom short. Drop in when the ember is far, plant, climb the boulder, Grow: a bloom puts out any ember it reaches, and its top is the way on.
tip Growth takes whatever stands inside it, ember or wanderer. Three generations make a bloom seven wide; the wall cut this one to five. Count three in from the open edge: the stone is right against the wall.
intro Something still burns down there, in a cave too low to stand tall in. Embers hate what grows. Plant beneath one and see.
outro The ember went out in the bloom. What grows again does not burn.
say wake|Spikes on the road. They do not move. That is their whole trick.
say plant|Now out, before it notices you. It is coming back.
say grow|Three generations. If the ember is inside them, it is over for it.
say found|Out. What grows again does not burn. The bridge past the vents does not hold; cross it running.
say die|The ember is faster than it looks. So are you, when you want to be.
